00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.000
Phillip: In this video we are going
to explain the benefits of innovation

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:05.560
and change for an organization.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.670
Maddy: Change is a fact of life and
organisations at the forefront of their

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.329
industry or line of service won’t stay
that way if they can’t adapt to change.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.349
Phillip: Innovation is when an organization
or business makes positive changes to

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.810
maintain its competitive edge and continue
to deliver quality products or services.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.219
Maddy: It’s important that organisations
and businesses embrace the fact that they

00:00:28.219 --> 00:00:32.970
need to change and innovate, as the world
around them is constantly moving, and it’s

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.569
necessary to innovate and change to keep pace.

00:00:36.029 --> 00:00:38.880
If not, they’ll find themselves falling behind.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.270
Phillip: Let’s look at some of the benefits
that can come from an organization or

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.680
business undergoing change and innovation.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.249
Maddy: Embracing new technology

00:00:48.769 --> 00:00:53.239
Every day, new technologies are being
invented or developed and new scientific

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.900
discoveries are being announced.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.870
Although sometimes it can take a while
for an important new kind of technology

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.570
to establish itself, many organisations
and businesses keep an eye out for the

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.870
next game-changing technological advance.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.779
By embracing new technology through innovation
and change, businesses and other organisations

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.730
can outcompete their rivals and satisfy
their customers’ needs more efficiently.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.340
Phillip: Cost savings

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:24.250
By changing and innovating, organisations can
keep down costs especially through adopting

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:29.800
new work or management practices where
inefficiencies are identified and removed.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.100
However sometimes this can involve
redundancies, not always a popular

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.249
change, especially when certain job
roles are found to no longer be needed.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.090
Maddy: Increased profits

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.060
This is the flipside of cost savings.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:48.280
By innovating and adapting, businesses and
organisations can increase the profits they’re

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.750
bringing in, which they can in tur, re-invest
into the business and reward their people.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.330
Phillip: Boosting efficiency

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.690
Innovation can help an organization or
business discover more efficient ways

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.500
to deliver its product and services.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.610
This can also help improve the customer
experience, making it more likely current

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.360
customers will stay loyal and spread
the good word about their experience.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.510
It also frees up time and resources for
the organization to achieve even more.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.090
Maddy: Competitiveness

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:23.610
For businesses, it’s always important to be as
competitive as possible, striving to do better

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.830
than other businesses in their field or industry.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.300
Innovation is very important
in staying competitive.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.190
If you’re not innovating, you can always
guarantee that one of your competitors is.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.430
This is also true of non-business
organisations who want to maintain a

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.860
good reputation and continue to deliver
their services and products effectively.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.790
Phillip: Willingness to experiment

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.490
It’s true that not all innovations and
changes achieve what they set out too.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:56.650
But by embracing innovation and change, and
recognizing that they’re inevitable parts of

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:03.470
life, you can inspire a spirit of experimentation
in your people, making them more open minded

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.470
and more willing to try new ideas in the future.

